{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When a quarter's contract demand cannot be fully met from that quarter's production plus beginning inventory, is the shortfall carried over as backorder (unmet demand) that must be satisfied in a later quarter, or is it simply lost (no penalty beyond the delay compensation already stated)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice between two mutually exclusive options (backlog vs. lost demand), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the delay compensation, is the penalty charged per quarter of delay (so a unit delivered 2 quarters late costs 2× the per-quarter rate), or is it a flat one-time penalty regardless of how many quarters late the unit is delivered?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice between two mutually exclusive compensation structures, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The end-of-quarter-4 inventory requirement of 150 units per product — does this 150 have to be on-hand (physical) inventory, or is it acceptable if some of it is offset by backorders (i.e., net inventory of 150, meaning you could have 200 on hand and 50 units still owed)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the definition of the inventory requirement (on-hand vs. net), presenting a binary choice within one semantic request."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The 15,000 production hours per quarter — is this a hard cap on total hours used (production hours for all three products combined must be ≤ 15,000 each quarter), or is it the total available hours that can be allocated, with the possibility of using fewer?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for the specific nature of the 15,000-hour constraint (hard cap vs. available capacity), which constitutes one semantically independent request."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The inventory holding cost of 5 yuan per unit per quarter — does this apply to all on-hand inventory at the end of each quarter (including the 150 units that must be held at the end of quarter 4), or only to inventory that exists in quarters 1–3 (i.e., is the end-of-quarter-4 inventory exempt from holding cost)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the scope of the inventory holding cost, specifically whether it applies to end-of-quarter-4 inventory."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The delay compensation is described as \"per unit per quarter delay\" — is this charged on the number of units that are backordered at the end of each quarter (i.e., the cumulative backorder level carried into the next quarter), or is it charged per unit based on the total number of quarters that specific unit was late before it was finally delivered?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice between two mutually exclusive calculation methods for delay compensation."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The delay compensation is charged per unit based on the total number of quarters that specific unit was late before it was finally delivered — does this mean a unit of product I demanded in quarter 1 but delivered in quarter 3 incurs a penalty of 2 × 20 = 40 yuan (2 quarters late), or 3 × 20 = 60 yuan (3 quarters from demand to delivery)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding how the delay penalty is calculated (late quarters vs. total quarters), presenting two mutually exclusive options for the same metric."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The inventory holding cost of 5 yuan per unit per quarter — is this charged on the on-hand inventory at the end of each quarter (i.e., the closing inventory level), or on the average inventory during the quarter, or on the total units that were produced but not delivered in that quarter?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the basis for calculating inventory holding costs, presenting three mutually exclusive options for one specific parameter."
}

